---
import Tunnel from '../../../layouts/Tunnel.astro';
import Choice from '../../../components/Choice.astro';
---
<Tunnel title="Nothing At All | Save My Gig!" status="No_Sound · Master" red>
  <div class="step-label">The master</div>
  <h2 style="margin-bottom:1rem">Check the master</h2>

  <ul class="checklist">
    <!-- Was "BOOTH and MASTER are two different knobs. Raise both." Every DJ
         and every tech on earth knows that. The instruction was fine, the
         explanation was the insult. -->
    <li>Raise <strong>MASTER</strong> to 12 o'clock. Raise <strong>BOOTH</strong> too.</li>
    <li>Check nothing is muted, and nothing is plugged into the <strong>master insert</strong>.</li>
  </ul>

  <!-- "Master insert" is native to a tech and foreign to plenty of DJs. The
       term stays, the explanation hides. Whoever already knows it never opens
       this and pays nothing for it being here. -->
  <details class="move-more" style="margin-bottom:1.25rem">
    <summary>What is the master insert</summary>
    <p>
      A patch point on the back of the mixer where an outboard processor sits in
      the master signal. If a cable is plugged in and nothing sends audio back,
      the master goes silent with every fader up. If something is patched in, it
      is almost certainly the venue's: ask before you pull it.
      <br /><br />
      Words for the tech: <strong>"There's something patched into the master
      insert. Is that live, or is it dead gear I can pull?"</strong>
    </p>
  </details>

  <p class="question">Sound in the room?</p>

  <Choice step="ns_master"
    a={{ href: '/saved?path=no_sound&branch=master', label: 'YES, IT PLAYS', event: 'outcome_reached', data: { outcome: 'saved', path: 'no_sound' } }}
    b={{ href: '/protocol/no-sound/master-2', label: 'NO, STILL SILENT' }}
  />
</Tunnel>
